WEBVTT

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:07.020
Our tale begins in the slightly distant past.

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:12.820
A young man traveled across the ocean to study music.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:20.280
Everything was a wonderful, new world for the young man.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.000
Then, one day, he had an extraordinary encounter.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:30.330
What he encountered was a very small and mysterious creature.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:37.200
The tiny creature was injured, so feeling pity for it, he treated it.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:44.310
The young man said that he dreamed of establishing a music school in his home country.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:47.970
I owe you my life.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:52.750
For this, I will grant the blessing of music to the school you build.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.850
Now, some time has passed.

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:02.540
Another extraordinary encounter awaits.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:41.590
An Unbelievable Prelude

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:44.510
Seiso Academy - Secondary School

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.510
Good morning.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.820
I want to hold a competition again this year.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:53.980
A school-wide music competition for the students of Seiso Academy.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.760
But, for some reason, no one notices me!

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.810
I overslept!

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.360
Ah! Yunoki-sama!

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.680
Hey!

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:31.900
At this rate, the competition will end up the same as it always does.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:35.520
Why does this town have so many hills?!

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.470
And stairs, too!

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.390
All right, practice is over!

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:58.380
Won't someone please hear my pleas?!

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.050
No way! First period already?!

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:12.710
Why is the schoolhouse way at the end of campus?

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:14.800
Why doesn't anyone notice me?

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.240
Huh? What's that?

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:29.540
Hey, can you see me?

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.450
You can, can't you?

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.960
Wh...What are you?

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.300
Awesome! I finally found you!

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:45.330
Now I can finally stage the competition!

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:57.990
The carillon's ringing.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:58.930
You're right!

00:04:58.930 --> 00:04:59.980
Then this year...

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:00.930
A competition?

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.860
Principal's Office

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:07.750
The carillon in the schoolyard rang earlier.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.670
We will be holding a school-wide music competition.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:15.010
So, Kanazawa-sensei, I'd like you to chair it.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:16.450
Me?

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:17.600
Yes.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.960
What a pain...

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.290
Oh, Kaho-chan!

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:28.070
What was that thing before?

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:30.870
Kaho-chan, listen, listen!

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:31.630
Huh?

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:35.110
It's nothing. Mio always gets like that.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:36.990
You're so mean, Nao-chan!

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:39.120
It's a tale of romance and dreams!

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.460
Violence romance, right?

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:43.620
Violin romance!

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.480
Listen, Kaho-chan!

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:50.760
The bell that rang before is the signal that we're having a school-wide music competition!

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:55.040
And, there's an incredibly romantic tradition that goes along with the competition!

00:05:56.190 --> 00:06:01.970
Twenty-five years ago, two contestants in the competition fell in love!

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:05.700
But the two were rivals for the grand prize.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:10.210
And then, they found a fairy who lives here at school in secret!

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.660
Fairy?

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:15.470
And the two of them were violinists!

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.810
What a load of crap.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.340
Class is about to begin.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.550
A fairy living in secret at the school?

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:26.660
No way! Fairies don't exist!

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:27.850
Hino-san?

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:30.560
I imagined it! Just my imagination!

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:30.550
Hino-san.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:31.200
Hino-san!

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.670
It was definitely my imagination!

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.920
Could it be the weather?

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.600
Come to the faculty room after class.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:43.530
Yes, ma'am.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.050
OK, bring that to class 2-A.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.880
She didn't need to loan me out to the other teachers...

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.010
But class A is in the Music Department, huh?

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.590
Man, that's so far away.

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:18.000
Watch yourself.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:21.700
Sorry... Are you all right?

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:26.420
Sorry I'm making you help me.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:29.610
It's fine. This is too much for you to carry alone.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.760
Since our ties are the same color, he must be a second-year, huh?

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.970
Huh? Something wrong?

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:40.340
Ah, I'm Kahoko Hino from class 2. How about you?

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:43.590
I'm Ryotaro Tsuchiura, from class 5.

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:45.570
Ah, here it is.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:48.530
General Studies students. Wonder what they're doing here?

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:51.450
I'm not sure we're welcomed here.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:54.760
We go to the same school and yet we're like strangers to them.

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:56.780
Mind moving?

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:00.330
You're in my way.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:02.430
Ah, I'm sorry.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:06.450
We were asked to carry these to this classroom.
Will you take them for us?

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:09.940
Go into the classroom and place them somewhere.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:13.980
Hey!

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.490
It doesn't concern me.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.680
What's with that jerk?

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:25.440
He's got a cute face, but he looks like the type to keep to himself.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:28.280
You really helped me there. Thanks!

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:31.170
It's nothing. Anyway, I'll be going ahead now.

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:33.480
OK! Many thanks!

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:40.200
I saw that weird thing this morning, but now I feel relieved.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:44.990
I've been looking for you, Kahoko Hino!

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.210
No way...

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.720
You've nothing to fear.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:53.320
The name's Lili, a musical fairy called a Fata-

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.500
Where'd she go?!

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:01.300
Oh, Kaho-chan.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:03.650
I know I didn't see that...

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:04.820
Is something wrong?

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:08.400
No, it's nothing... Eh?

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.720
Looking at me and then running away is cruel!

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:13.170
Kaho?

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:14.380
Uh, that...

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.800
What?

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.870
Sorry, but you're the only one who can see me.

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:22.860
N-No way...

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:27.570
My, things have gotten interesting!

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:33.050
The Seiso Academy music competition where they say the victor is granted the blessing of music.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:38.810
It must be fate that they're holding this while I, Nami Amo, am in the Journalism Club!

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.960
I'll report on every bit of it!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.570
Yunoki-sama, would you like some after-lunch herb tea?

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.850
Yes, please.

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:57.690
The ones tending to Yunoki today are first years, huh?

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:02.330
They're chosen on a daily rotation from the Yunoki Guard, right?

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:06.360
Man, Yunoki is incredible. I could never pull something like that off.

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:08.120
Who could?

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.820
Kaho-chan, are you still not feeling well?

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:16.750
No, I'm feeling a bit better.

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:19.100
Umm, hello, everybody.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:26.550
I'm sure you've heard by now, but we'll be holding a school-wide music competition this year.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:31.360
I will now announce the participants of the competition.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:37.690
First, from Class 3-B in the Music Department...

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.280
Azuma Yunoki-kun.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:56.050
You did it, Yunoki! Congrats!

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:58.600
Thank you, Hihara.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:00.160
Give it your all, Yunoki!

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.270
I will.

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:05.600
Thank you, everyone.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.560
From the same class, 3-B...

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.800
Kazuki Hihara-kun.

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:19.540
What? Me too?

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:20.900
You did it, Hihara!

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:22.270
You rascal!

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:24.360
Congratulations, Hihara.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:28.040
Thanks! Let's both do our best!

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.160
Next, from class 2-B...

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.750
Len Tsukimori-kun.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:41.930
I knew it.

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:44.600
Oh, Tsukimori-kun. Congratulations...

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.220
You're so amazing.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:51.150
What's amazing about it? I was merely chosen to participate.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:53.350
And then, from class 1-A...

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.240
Keiichi Shimizu-kun.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.450
What?!

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:10.490
Hey, Shimizu, they chose you.

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.430
They did?

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:18.550
Class 1-B, Shoko Fuyuumi-san.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:36.150
They picked you even though you're only a first year! That's incredible!

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.470
No way... What should I do...

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:40.520
And lastly, from General Studies class 2-2...

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:41.240
What?!

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:42.820
Kahoko Hino-san.

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:46.570
M-Me?!

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.060
Kaho-chan?

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:49.620
Did he say Hino?

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:53.590
Why... me?

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:08.100
Kanazawa-sensei!

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:11.440
Hmm? Do you need something?

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:14.650
I'm Hino, a second year...

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:17.890
Hino? Oh, the participant.

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:23.810
About that... Is there some sort of mix-up and that's why I was chosen?

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:26.690
Nope. It's you, all right.

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:27.650
But...

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:32.480
If you were chosen, then you must have seen IT, right?

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.520
It? Do you mean...

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:38.730
Can you see him too, Sensei?!

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:40.520
Me? Not at all.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:43.800
The Principal just told me to tell you that.

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:47.820
Oh, right. There was a message from IT to you.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:48.740
Huh?

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:52.330
Come to the Music Department's practice room after school today.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:53.330
U-Umm...

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:54.800
Kannayan!

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:56.690
We were chosen to participate!

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:01.220
We heard you were chairing the competition, so we came to introduce ourselves.

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:04.930
Hey! Are you the girl from General Studies?

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:09.970
I'm Kazuki Hihara, a third year. I play the trumpet.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:10.910
Nice to meet you!

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:11.570
Umm...

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:15.940
I'm kinda happy they chose someone from General Studies.

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:18.060
I bet it's gonna be a ton of fun.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:23.350
Now, now, Hihara. You've got to let the girl at least get a word in.

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:24.920
Ah, sorry!

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:28.140
I'm really sorry.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:32.360
I'm Azuma Yunoki. I play the flute.

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:35.840
Ah, he's so beautiful...

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:39.120
Your name was Hino-san, right? What instrument do you play?

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.150
Umm...

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:44.410
Don't say the flute. That'd mean I'd have another rival.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:46.240
N-No, actually...

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.920
Wait, is it the trumpet?!

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.030
Actually...

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.590
It's a big misunderstanding!

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:52.700
Please excuse me!

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.620
Ah, Hino-san!

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:03.880
Class 2-2 Kahoko Hino

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:09.340
This is the first time I've gone to the practice room.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:17.240
Is IT really going to be here?

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.730
You came, Kahoko Hino.

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:36.240
I-I-It's really here!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.590
Who on earth are you?

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:43.540
The name's Lili. I'm called a Fata, a music fairy.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:46.790
Fata? A music fairy?

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:50.940
Just think of Fata as the source of happiness within music.

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:55.160
So, in order to fill the world with happiness,

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:58.600
we spread music all over the world.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:03.290
In the old days, lots of humans could see us.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:09.320
But, times have changed. The people nowadays can't sense our presence.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:11.190
But, you're different.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:14.450
You can see me!

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:17.760
That means you must have an affinity for Fatas.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:19.910
You're on the same wavelength as us.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:24.420
That means you are harboring some latent musical abilities.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.800
That's why you were chosen for the competition!

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:30.870
How dare you force me to participate in it!

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:35.260
Don't the characters for "music" in your language, Japanese, mean "to enjoy sound"?

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.470
Everyone can enjoy music.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:41.260
I want you to feel music deeper within you!

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:42.130
But...

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:44.670
I shall grant you this!

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.660
That's a magical violin.

00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:05.880
Magical... violin?

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:11.300
I've spent many years researching to perfect it. It's a wonderful violin!

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:13.670
And, with the hidden magical powers within it,

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:17.520
anyone can play it!

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:20.140
Anyone can play it?

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:25.330
Then you could have picked someone else!

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:28.420
S-See, since it's just a prototype,

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:33.180
there's a chance it won't work unless the person has an affinity for us.

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:35.280
So I'm your guinea pig?

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:39.620
Anyway, how about you try and play it?

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.540
You can use this bow.

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:49.340
But I don't know how to play a violin.

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:51.510
Just do what you've seen before.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:54.200
Even so...

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.470
Let's see... I think it went like...

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:10.730
N-No!

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:13.210
What did you do that for?!

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:16.190
B-B-Because my body just moved on its own!

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:20.120
That's a very valuable violin!

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.070
I don't need this thing.

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:24.150
"This thing"?

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:28.060
Here, I'll throw in a case.

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:30.170
What is this, an infomercial?

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:31.470
You don't want it?

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:32.490
Of course not!

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:34.500
Am I bothering you?

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:35.420
Absolutely.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.590
Wh-Why?

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:40.540
You were chosen because you're special!

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.250
Really? Me?

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.820
I shall grant you this magical violin!

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:46.610
My, how wonderful!

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:50.010
Together, let's fill the world with music!

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:51.390
I'll give it everything I have.

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:53.870
That's the reaction I expected!

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:55.490
Not gonna happen.

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.980
Anyway, I've already chosen you.

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:12.770
I'm counting on you, Kahoko Hino.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:15.950
Hey! Wait!

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:18.270
Wait...

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.510
No way...

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:23.260
Hey.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.680
Huh?

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:28.430
What's a General Studies student doing here?

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:30.480
Oh, this boy...

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:34.300
I've reserved this room for the rest of the day.

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:36.060
Can you leave, please?

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:38.440
I don't want to waste precious practice time.

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:40.080
Ah, I'm sorry!

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:52.130
So they're having a competition this year, huh?

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:54.850
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:59.000
Plus a General Studies student is entering. It's gonna be awesome.

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:04.020
I just hope I don't have to do much.

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:12.140
What should I do with this?

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:14.190
This is absolutely insane.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:20.390
A first-year with no special talent being chosen for the competition? It's repugnant.

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:22.860
Who are those girls?

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:25.680
You need to understand the level that you're at.

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:28.580
You'd best turn the offer down immediately, for your own sake.

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:31.460
Do you have anything to say, Fuyuumi-san?

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:35.810
Excuse me, what are you doing?

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:37.960
What's it to you?

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:41.460
Oh, she's the General Studies student who was picked for the competition.

00:20:41.730 --> 00:20:45.230
Beyond that, they picked a pretty homely looking girl, wouldn't you say?

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.550
Wh-What's their problem?

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:51.710
And, this one here is dull too.

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:54.810
It's a disgrace for the Music Department.

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:56.200
It really is.

00:20:56.200 --> 00:20:58.370
Aren't you the bigger disgraces?!

00:20:58.370 --> 00:21:01.770
You're just picking on her because you weren't chosen!

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:03.380
What did you say?

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:05.150
Whoops!

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:10.580
Well, since you were chosen, why don't you play a moving piece for us right now?

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:12.790
Huh? A-Actually...

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:15.840
What? You can't play?

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:20.120
If that's the case, why don't you take back what you said and apologize?

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:22.740
Down on your knees.

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.490
That's...

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:27.180
What's it gonna be, Ms. General Studies?

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.750
Wh-What should I do?

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:34.260
That's a magical violin. Anyone can play it.

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:40.600
That's right. If he's telling an amateur like me to enter the competition, then I should be able to...

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:43.330
What's your answer, Ms. General Studies?

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:45.450
Fine. I'll play.

00:23:36.630 --> 00:23:39.530
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:42.770
Lili's One Point Classic

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:43.130
I'm going to teach you little tidbits about music!

00:23:43.130 --> 00:23:46.580
Today, I'll introduce you to the violin.

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:51.420
The violin was created in 16th century northern Italy.

00:23:51.420 --> 00:23:55.280
It makes sound by moving a bow over its four strings!

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:57.800
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:57.800 --> 00:24:02.710
Since the violin is expensive and beautiful, what other name could it go by?

00:24:02.710 --> 00:24:05.540
The answer is at the end of this program!

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:07.580
How did I get myself into this mess?

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:09.590
Next Episode

00:24:07.580 --> 00:24:10.590
I can't believe I have to perform in front of everyone!

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:13.140
Your skills aren't even worth mentioning.

00:24:13.140 --> 00:24:15.920
Don't say such things during the next episode preview!

00:24:15.920 --> 00:24:18.290
Next episode: The Impending Troubles of Gavotte.

00:24:18.290 --> 00:24:20.550
What's Gavotte?

00:24:21.060 --> 00:24:22.310
The answer is...

00:24:23.070 --> 00:24:25.550
The Queen of Musical Instruments!
